From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:59:08 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] fds-disk

SELECT+L2, the PlayStation disc chord, flips a Famicom disk to its next
side on the Disk System shelf. fceumm registers no libretro disk
control at this pin: it ejects or inserts on a press of the pad's R and
selects the next side on a press of L, only while the disk is out. slot
keeps L1 and R1 for itself on this shelf and presses the core's own R,
then L two frames later, then R again 60 frames after the eject, so a
game polling the drive sees the disk out for a second. The walk goes
through every side of every disk and back to the first (Disk 1 Side A,
Disk 1 Side B, Disk 2 Side A, ...). The side in the drive is read back
from the core's own state (SELD), never counted by slot, so a loaded
state or a rewind cannot put the banner out of step, and the banner
names it. A one-sided disk is not flipped. The PlayStation disc path is
not used for disks.
